# DAX measures | Aggregate row expressions and define ratios. | Create revenue and weighted margin measures in a product matrix.
Iterators | SUMX evaluates an expression per row in the current context. Multiplying separate sums of price and quantity does not equal a sum of line revenues. | SUMX; Row context; Filter context | Revenue = SUMX(Sales, Sales[Quantity]*Sales[UnitPrice]) | Lines 2×10 and 3×5 yield 35. | Finance calculates actual line-level revenue. | Add a negative returned quantity and reconcile the total.
Safe ratios | DIVIDE handles a zero denominator. Choose blank for undefined rates unless a documented business rule requires an alternative. | DIVIDE; BLANK; Weighted rate | Margin % = DIVIDE([Revenue]-[Cost],[Revenue]) | Revenue 50 and cost 40 gives 20%; zero revenue yields blank. | Profitability reports avoid misleading empty-selection percentages. | Compare total margin with the average of product margins.
